        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-25512",
        ":question/problem": "Find the range of the function $f(x)=-2\\operatorname{sin}(3x)+1.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The range of $\\operatorname{sin}x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}(3x)\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-2$ and then adding $1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\operatorname{sin}(3x)\\le 1 \\\\  & 2\\ge -2\\operatorname{sin}(2x)\\ge -2 \\\\  & 3\\ge -2\\operatorname{sin}(2x)+1\\ge -1 \\\\  & -1\\le f(x)\\le 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)\\in [-1,3].$"
      },
      {
        ":db/id": 17592186234034,
