        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-40903",
        ":question/problem": "What is the range of $f(x)=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+2?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The range of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $3$ and then adding $2$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\le 1 \\\\  & -3\\le 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})\\le 3 \\\\  & -1\\le 3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x+\\frac{\\pi }{6})+2\\le 5 \\\\  & -1\\le f(x)\\le 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $f(x)\\in [-1,5].$"
