        ":question/math-academy-id": "q-41964",
        ":question/problem": "What is the range of the function $y=-4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{30}^{∘})+1?$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "The range of $\\operatorname{cos}⁡x$ is\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHorizontal shifts and stretches have no effect on the range. Therefore,\n\n$$\n-1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{30}^{∘})\\le 1.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the above inequality by $-4$ and then adding $1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & -1\\le \\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{30}^{∘})\\le 1 \\\\  & 4\\ge -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{30}^{∘})\\ge -4 \\\\  & 5\\ge -4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(x-{30}^{∘})+1\\ge -3 \\\\  & -3\\le y\\le 5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the range is $y\\in [-3,5].$"
